# Everything here is either a secret, a host-specific build artefact, or bulk that makes the
# build context slower to send for no gain. `__pycache__` earns its line twice over: this
# working tree keeps stale ones from other branches (a `src/identity/__pycache__` survives a
# checkout that removed `src/identity` itself), and copying those into an image would ship
# bytecode for modules that are not there.
.env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.git/
tests/
